From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: G81EM1 bring-up <g81em1@localhost>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:05:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] lineage-sdk: start external services from their inspected
 instance

LineageSystemServer creates every external service once to inspect its feature
declaration, then asks SystemServiceManager to create another instance by
class. Services that publish a binder in their constructor therefore replace
the first binder before its onStart() runs. On this device that leaves
StyleInterfaceService with a null overlay manager and crashes LineageParts
when an accent is selected.

Start the already inspected instance so its constructor and onStart execute on
the same object. This also removes duplicate binder registration for the other
Lineage external services.
---
 .../org/lineageos/platform/internal/LineageSystemServer.java   | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/LineageSystemServer.java b/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/LineageSystemServer.java
index 0bf7c95e..00000000 100644
--- a/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/LineageSystemServer.java
+++ b/lineage/lib/main/java/org/lineageos/platform/internal/LineageSystemServer.java
@@ -82,6 +82,6 @@ public class LineageSystemServer {
                     } else {
                         Slog.i(TAG, "Starting service " + service);
-                        ssm.startService(lineageSystemService.getClass());
+                        ssm.startService(lineageSystemService);
                     }
                 } else {
                     Slog.i(TAG, "Not starting service " + service +
